# Atlas Definition of Done

This is the **minimum quality gate** for every Atlas milestone. A milestone is incomplete until every item below is satisfied or explicitly deferred with approval in the Build Manifest / decision log.

Do not begin the next milestone until this gate passes and **approval is recorded**.

## Visual & responsive

- [ ] Matches approved Figma compositions for the milestone (Figma is visual source of truth — see `atlas-design`)
- [ ] Validated at **Desktop (1440)**, **Tablet (768)**, and **Mobile (390)**
- [ ] Responsive recomposition matches Figma (not stacked desktop)
- [ ] No unapproved design drift during implementation

## Accessibility

- [ ] WCAG **AA** — axe clear of serious/critical on delivered routes
- [ ] Keyboard path, focus order, skip link, and landmarks verified
- [ ] `prefers-reduced-motion` respected where motion exists

## Tests & build

- [ ] Playwright coverage for delivered routes/journeys (see `atlas-testing`)
- [ ] Visual regression baselines for stable D/T/M views
- [ ] TypeScript / typecheck passing for affected packages
- [ ] Production build passing for affected packages

## Architecture & engineering policy

- [ ] Architecture unchanged unless the change was **explicitly approved** (see `atlas-frontend` freeze policy)
- [ ] **Rule of Two** validated for any new shared extraction
- [ ] **Rule of Stability** validated (no extract that destabilizes frozen routes)
- [ ] **Fixture First** preserved until approved Strapi mappers exist
- [ ] Domain types stay at the content boundary — no CMS DTOs in UI
- [ ] No speculative abstractions (see `no-overengineering`)

## Documentation & release control

- [ ] Build Manifest updated (status, scope, checklist)
- [ ] Implementation report written for the milestone
- [ ] Architecture report updated when boundaries, ownership, or freeze scope change
- [ ] Deferred technical debt recorded (not silently dropped)
- [ ] Decision log updated for material trade-offs
- [ ] Product docs screenshots/links stay in sync when visuals change (see `atlas-documentation`)

## Gate

```text
Milestone complete  →  DoD satisfied + approval recorded  →  next milestone may begin
```
